# An allowlist: everything is left out of the build context unless named
# below, so a new file or directory (a cache, a report, an .env) never reaches
# the image by default. What must never be in it: .git, the golden and eval
# packages, fixtures/, tests/, environment files, the eval response cache
# (.cache/), eval/, .scratch/, .claude/, .venv and every other local cache.
# tests/docker/test_dockerignore.py checks both directions.
*

# The project and its lock.
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!.python-version

# The service's source, and the template render fills at run time.
!src/
!templates/fictitious_recruitment.docx

# Never, even under an allowed path: the golden set and the eval (neither is
# imported by the service), environment files, bytecode and build leftovers.
src/cvr/golden/
src/cvr/eval/
**/.env*
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
